  Refs #33; Refs #26. Unit YM-000033.

  <section|Established local result><label|established-local-result>

  The section derives the selected right inverse and its convergence from the
  displayed finite-volume inputs, proves sensor convergence, and obtains the
  eventual uniform receiver bound and weighted Ward defect. The marked-field
  and scalar Ward limits remain distinct.

  <section|Retained inputs and review status><label|retained-inputs-and-review-status>

  The precise upstream inputs and their source suppliers remain in the
  mathematical text and correspondence. Their complete quantitative
  production and the full existence argument are not asserted here. The unit
  is a draft with null formal review approvals. Agent assistance does not
  establish responsible human acceptance. Fresh pinned Lean elaboration and
  target-specific axiom/kernel replay remain unrun; source audit work is
  separately owned in #37.

  <section|Integration><label|integration>

  Match the same chart, norms, weights and receiver parameters in the
  downstream Scribe argument; resolve its chapter order and parent-owned
  evidence references.

  The main assembly, supporting chapters, shared metadata, pinned Lean source
  and dependencies are unchanged by this contribution. Review the exact
  target version before integration. Actual local checks and their limits are
  recorded in validation.md.

  <section|2026-11-13 revision for #126 and
  #127><label|2026-11-13-revision-for-126-and-127>

  The current bounded author revision responds to R1\UR5 in the response
  table in <verbatim|correspondence.md>. It starts from upstream
  <verbatim|84a6a9371caddd2f9967b9d6924e156ec097610e>; the earlier
  independent review fingerprint is stale for the changed text. It leaves all
  prior review reports and approval metadata untouched. Fresh independent
  mathematics and Lean-correspondence review at the new fingerprint is
  required. The selected chart, tested-map, transport, medium/probe and
  common-data producers remain conditional inputs; the wrapper's two external
  reference warnings are documented rather than hidden. See
  <verbatim|validation.md> for checks actually run and their limits. No push,
  draft PR, public comment, claim release or human acceptance is asserted by
  this local revision.

